---
// Canonical copy: docs/builds/autonomous-seo-agent.md (edit there, then regenerate this body).
// Static page on purpose — see the note in src/content.config.ts (a content collection
// here busted the build cache and blew Vercel's 45-minute Hobby build timeout).
// Video-first: the walkthrough carries the detail, so this page stays short.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Autonomous SEO Agent';
const status = 'LIVE';
const date = 'October 2026';
const summary =
  'An AI agent that finds five new website opportunities daily, creates professional profiles, verifies accounts through its own Gmail inbox, and tracks everything without manual intervention.';
const stack = ['HyperAgent', 'AI Agents', 'Automation', 'SEO', 'Gmail'];
const videoId = '_MAhfwQxdvA';
const videoUrl = `https://youtu.be/${videoId}`;
const videoTitle = 'I Gave an AI Agent an SEO Job. Now It Works Without Me.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description="How I built an autonomous HyperAgent workflow that researches five new websites a day, creates profiles, verifies them through its own Gmail inbox, and tracks every result. Watch the demo."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Building', path: '/building/' },
    { name: title, path: '/building/autonomous-seo-agent/' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="build">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/building/"><span aria-hidden="true">&larr;</span> Building</a>
    </nav>

    <header class="build-header">
      <p class="page-mark" aria-hidden="true">// build</p>
      <div class="title-row">
        <h1>{title}</h1>
        <span class={`badge badge-${status.toLowerCase()}`}>
          <span class="badge-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          {status}
        </span>
      </div>
      <p class="summary">{summary}</p>
      <p class="meta">
        <span class="meta-key">{status === 'LIVE' ? 'Live since' : 'Shipped'}</span>
        {date}
      </p>
      <ul class="stack" aria-label="Stack">
        {stack.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>Building a presence across the web is slow, repetitive work: find a legitimate directory or profile site, check that it is free and relevant, sign up, confirm the email, fill in the same bio and links again, and write down what happened. I wanted an agent to do that job every day without me in the loop.</p>

      <h2 id="demo">Watch the demo</h2>
      <figure class="video">
        <div class="video-frame">
          <iframe
            src={`https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/${videoId}?rel=0`}
            title={`Ken Ashe: ${videoTitle}`}
            width="560"
            height="315"
            loading="lazy"
            allow="accelerometer; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
            allowfullscreen
            referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
          ></iframe>
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          <a href={videoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Watch on YouTube ↗</a>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>Every day the agent researches five new candidate websites and decides whether each one qualifies: a legitimate, relevant, free listing. Link farms, paid placements and spam are out.</p>
      <p>For each qualified site it attempts a signup on its own. It creates the account, opens its dedicated inbox to confirm the verification email, and completes the profile. If a site needs something it cannot do alone, it skips that site and moves on. I do not review or approve individual signups.</p>
      <p>Every opportunity is logged as researched, attempted, completed or skipped, so the next run never repeats work and I can see exactly what happened.</p>

      <h2>Tools and architecture</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>HyperAgent</strong> runs the agent on a daily schedule, with a browser for research and signups.</li>
        <li><strong>A dedicated Gmail account</strong> handles signups and verification, separate from my personal email.</li>
        <li><strong>A reusable profile kit</strong> keeps every listing consistent: bios, credentials, headshots and website links.</li>
        <li><strong>A tracker table</strong> records each site, its status and the live profile URL.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>None of this is specific to HyperAgent. The same pattern (a daily research step, a dedicated inbox, a profile kit and a tracker) could be built on other agent platforms.</p>

      <h2>Initial results</h2>
      <p>So far the agent has researched 63 websites. Researching a site is not the same as registering on it: of those, eight new profiles are confirmed live, created and verified end to end by the agent, including Peerlist, Wellfound, Devpost, Contra, Codeberg and Speaker Deck. The rest were rejected, skipped or are still queued.</p>

      <h2>Limitations</h2>
      <p>Some sites cannot be completed automatically. They require Google-only sign-in, a business email, phone or ID verification, a paid plan, or a CAPTCHA the agent cannot clear, so it skips them and records why.</p>
      <p>I have not established any SEO impact. Most of these profiles carry nofollow links, and whether they help search visibility over time is an open question this build does not answer.</p>

      <p><a href={videoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Watch the full walkthrough on YouTube ↗</strong></a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .build {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .crumbs {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
  }
  .crumbs a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 150ms ease;
  }
  .crumbs a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .page-mark {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .title-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
  }
  .build-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  /* Status badge: same treatment as the Building cards. */
  .badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45em;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    padding: 0.3rem 0.55rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    white-space: nowrap;
    background-color: var(--bg);
  }
  .badge-dot {
    width: 0.4rem;
    height: 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background-color: currentColor;
  }
  .badge-live {
    color: var(--accent-2);
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent-2) 35%, var(--border));
  }
  .badge-live .badge-dot {
    background-color: var(--accent-2);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent-2) 18%, transparent);
  }
  .badge-shipped {
    color: #94a3b8;
    border-color: rgb(100 116 139 / 0.2);
    background-color: rgb(100 116 139 / 0.1);
  }
  .badge-shipped .badge-dot {
    background-color: #64748b;
  }
  .summary {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }
  .meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .meta-key {
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    margin-right: 0.4rem;
  }
  .stack {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 3rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .stack li {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    background-color: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.55rem;
  }

  /* Markdown body */
  .prose {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .prose :global(h2) {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 1.875rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 2.75rem 0 1rem;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .prose :global(h2::before) {
    content: '// ';
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7em;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    vertical-align: 0.15em;
  }
  .prose :global(p) {
    margin: 0 0 1.15rem;
  }
  .prose :global(strong) {
